ext","value":"A sync insert did not clear the key's pending local layers. After a confirmed insert, the next remote update reported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$origin: 'local'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optimistic-history grammar: source rows are written as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"insert"},{"type":"text","value":" for a key the source lacks."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"B2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A sync delete did not clear the key's pending local layers. A later source reinsert reported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$origin: 'local'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Optimistic-history grammar: source deletes. Pinned replay of the random-campaign counterexample."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"F2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A sync "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"write()"},{"type":"text","value":" after "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commit()"},{"type":"text","value":", while the batch waited for persistence, joined the queued batch."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retention oracle: a write to a committed, waiting batch throws "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"SyncTransactionAlreadyCommittedWriteError"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"G4"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup with a pending subset load emitted a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"start"},{"type":"text","value":" transition."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup/restart oracle: one "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"end"},{"type":"text","value":" transition at cleanup."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"H3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Idle cleanup that rescheduled itself could not be canceled by a returning subscriber, so the Collection cleaned up early."}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"New "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-idle-cleanup.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":", with a controllable browser idle scheduler."}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"grammar-change","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Grammar change"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Every optimistic-history source batch wrote "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"update"},{"type":"text","value":" messages, which act as\nupserts. The production "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"insert"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"},{"type":"text","value":" apply paths never ran in those\nhistories. The driver now tracks which keys the source holds, including\nqueued batches, in write order:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A row for an absent key is written as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"insert"},{"type":"text","value":". Later copies are updates."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A batch may carry "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"deletes"},{"type":"text","value":". Only keys the source holds apply."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The model receives the same resolved batch and removes deleted keys from\nits base. A source delete acknowledges no request."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A runtime witness requires 40 fixed-campaign histories to write source inserts\nand deletes. The extended grammar passes on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"main"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retention owner, B4 applied"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3 of 97 fail"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retention owner, B2 applied"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"the pinned replay fails; the fixed campaign does not reach it"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Retention owner, F2 applied"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1 of 97 fail"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Cleanup/restart owner, G4 applied"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1 of 41 fail"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Idle-cleanup owner, H3 applied"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1 of 1 fail"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"survivors-that-change-no-observation","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Survivors that change no observation"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"These were classified with evidence and need no witness. The port can delete\nthe code under the last two."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A2 to A4: the truncate reapply search and filter are dead."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"G1, G3, H2, I3: stale state that every reader ignores, or a cancellation that\nis a no-op on every reached history."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"D1, D3: the recompute delete filter's inner branch ran 0 times in 7,871\ntests and in targeted histories. Recompute keeps optimistic layers for keys\nwith pending sync operations, so no such delete forms."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"limits","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Limits"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"H3 depends on a browser idle scheduler. The suite's Node polyfill always\nreports a timed-out deadline."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Source deletes run only after a batch's rows. A delete before an insert of\nthe same key in one batch is outside the grammar."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The driver drops a source delete for a key the source lacks, so the grammar\nnever sends one. On a plain Collection, such a delete is a silent no-op. Its\neffect on an optimistic layer for the same key is unverified. The\noptimistic-history oracle owns that open cell; it needs the contract for the\nabsent-key delete and a witness with an active and an accepted request on\nthe key."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The idle-cleanup test needs per-file module isolation, the Vitest default.\nWithout it, the binding check fails with an explicit error."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The fallback that derives previous "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$synced"},{"type":"text","value":"/"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"$origin"},{"type":"text","value":" from completed\nrequest keys still has a survivor (see the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"2026-10-02-insert-for-absent-key.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"absent-key insert review"}]},{"type":"text","value":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"verification","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verification"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db"},{"type":"text","value":" Vitest, typecheck off: 201 files, 7,862 tests. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsc --noEmit"},{"type":"text","value":"\nreports only the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tests/conformance"},{"type":"text","value":" errors that need a built "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"dist"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"state-stack-mutation-round-test-gaps","text":"State-stack mutation round: test gaps","level":1},{"id":"how-the-gaps-were-found","text":"How the gaps were found","level":2},{"id":"grammar-change","text":"Grammar change","level":2},{"id":"survivors-that-change-no-observation","text":"Survivors that change no observation","level":2},{"id":"limits","text":"Limits","level":2},{"id":"verification","text":"Verification","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# State-stack mutation round: test gaps\n\nReviewed executable revision: `f1a40e58d` (base\n`ef1e6a4aa`). No production code changes.\n\n## How the gaps were found\n\nA planned code-weight refactor of `state.ts`, `sync.ts`, and `lifecycle.ts`\nhas nine prototype commits. Before porting them, 22 plausible porting mistakes\nwere applied to unchanged `main` as source mutants. Each survivor of the db\nsuite was then classified with a probe that passes on `main` and fails on the\nmutant, or with evidence that the mutant changes no public observation. Two\nsurvivors exposed bugs on `main`, which have separate repairs: a direct\nmutation confirmed inside its handler (#1986) and an update sent for an\nabsent key (#1995). This change closes five survivors that were test gaps.\n\n| Mutant | Wrong behavior that passed the suite | New witness |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| B4 | A sync insert did not clear the key's pending local layers. After a confirmed insert, the next remote update reported `$origin: 'local'`. | Optimistic-history grammar: source rows are written as `insert` for a key the source lacks. |\n| B2 | A sync delete did not clear the key's pending local layers. A later source reinsert reported `$origin: 'local'`. | Optimistic-history grammar: source deletes. Pinned replay of the random-campaign counterexample. |\n| F2 | A sync `write()` after `commit()`, while the batch waited for persistence, joined the queued batch. | Retention oracle: a write to a committed, waiting batch throws `SyncTransactionAlreadyCommittedWriteError`. |\n| G4 | Cleanup with a pending subset load emitted a `start` transition. | Cleanup/restart oracle: one `end` transition at cleanup. |\n| H3 | Idle cleanup that rescheduled itself could not be canceled by a returning subscriber, so the Collection cleaned up early. | New `collection-idle-cleanup.test.ts`, with a controllable browser idle scheduler. |\n\n## Grammar change\n\nEvery optimistic-history source batch wrote `update` messages, which act as\nupserts. The production `insert` and `delete` apply paths never ran in those\nhistories. The driver now tracks which keys the source holds, including\nqueued batches, in write order:\n\n- A row for an absent key is written as `insert`. Later copies are updates.\n- A batch may carry `deletes`. Only keys the source holds apply.\n- The model receives the same resolved batch and removes deleted keys from\n  its base. A source delete acknowledges no request.\n\nA runtime witness requires 40 fixed-campaign histories to write source inserts\nand deletes. The extended grammar passes on `main`.\n\n| Run | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Retention owner, B4 applied | 3 of 97 fail |\n| Retention owner, B2 applied | the pinned replay fails; the fixed campaign does not reach it |\n| Retention owner, F2 applied | 1 of 97 fail |\n| Cleanup/restart owner, G4 applied | 1 of 41 fail |\n| Idle-cleanup owner, H3 applied | 1 of 1 fail |\n\n## Survivors that change no observation\n\nThese were classified with evidence and need no witness. The port can delete\nthe code under the last two.\n\n- A2 to A4: the truncate reapply search and filter are dead.\n- G1, G3, H2, I3: stale state that every reader ignores, or a cancellation that\n  is a no-op on every reached history.\n- D1, D3: the recompute delete filter's inner branch ran 0 times in 7,871\n  tests and in targeted histories. Recompute keeps optimistic layers for keys\n  with pending sync operations, so no such delete forms.\n\n## Limits\n\n- H3 depends on a browser idle scheduler. The suite's Node polyfill always\n  reports a timed-out deadline.\n- Source deletes run only after a batch's rows. A delete before an insert of\n  the same key in one batch is outside the grammar.\n- The driver drops a source delete for a key the source lacks, so the grammar\n  never sends one. On a plain Collection, such a delete is a silent no-op. Its\n  effect on an optimistic layer for the same key is unverified. The\n  optimistic-history oracle owns that open cell; it needs the contract for the\n  absent-key delete and a witness with an active and an accepted request on\n  the key.\n- The idle-cleanup test needs per-file module isolation, the Vitest default.\n  Without it, the binding check fails with an explicit error.\n- The fallback that derives previous `$synced`/`$origin` from completed\n  request keys still has a survivor (see the\n  [absent-key insert review](2026-10-02-insert-for-absent-key.md)).\n\n## Verification\n\n`packages/db` Vitest, typecheck off: 201 files, 7,862 tests. `tsc --noEmit`\nreports only the `tests/conformance` errors that need a built `dist`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# State-stack mutation round: test gaps\n\nReviewed executable revision: `f1a40e58d` (base\n`ef1e6a4aa`). No production code changes.\n\n## How the gaps were found\n\nA planned code-weight refactor of `state.ts`, `sync.ts`, and `lifecycle.ts`\nhas nine prototype commits. Before porting them, 22 plausible porting mistakes\nwere applied to unchanged `main` as source mutants. Each survivor of the db\nsuite was then classified with a probe that passes on `main` and fails on the\nmutant, or with evidence that the mutant changes no public observation. Two\nsurvivors exposed bugs on `main`, which have separate repairs: a direct\nmutation confirmed inside its handler (#1986) and an update sent for an\nabsent key (#1995). This change closes five survivors that were test gaps.\n\n| Mutant | Wrong behavior that passed the suite | New witness |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| B4 | A sync insert did not clear the key's pending local layers. After a confirmed insert, the next remote update reported `$origin: 'local'`. | Optimistic-history grammar: source rows are written as `insert` for a key the source lacks. |\n| B2 | A sync delete did not clear the key's pending local layers. A later source reinsert reported `$origin: 'local'`. | Optimistic-history grammar: source deletes. Pinned replay of the random-campaign counterexample. |\n| F2 | A sync `write()` after `commit()`, while the batch waited for persistence, joined the queued batch. | Retention oracle: a write to a committed, waiting batch throws `SyncTransactionAlreadyCommittedWriteError`. |\n| G4 | Cleanup with a pending subset load emitted a `start` transition. | Cleanup/restart oracle: one `end` transition at cleanup. |\n| H3 | Idle cleanup that rescheduled itself could not be canceled by a returning subscriber, so the Collection cleaned up early. | New `collection-idle-cleanup.test.ts`, with a controllable browser idle scheduler. |\n\n## Grammar change\n\nEvery optimistic-history source batch wrote `update` messages, which act as\nupserts. The production `insert` and `delete` apply paths never ran in those\nhistories. The driver now tracks which keys the source holds, including\nqueued batches, in write order:\n\n- A row for an absent key is written as `insert`. Later copies are updates.\n- A batch may carry `deletes`. Only keys the source holds apply.\n- The model receives the same resolved batch and removes deleted keys from\n  its base. A source delete acknowledges no request.\n\nA runtime witness requires 40 fixed-campaign histories to write source inserts\nand deletes. The extended grammar passes on `main`.\n\n| Run | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Retention owner, B4 applied | 3 of 97 fail |\n| Retention owner, B2 applied | the pinned replay fails; the fixed campaign does not reach it |\n| Retention owner, F2 applied | 1 of 97 fail |\n| Cleanup/restart owner, G4 applied | 1 of 41 fail |\n| Idle-cleanup owner, H3 applied | 1 of 1 fail |\n\n## Survivors that change no observation\n\nThese were classified with evidence and need no witness. The port can delete\nthe code under the last two.\n\n- A2 to A4: the truncate reapply search and filter are dead.\n- G1, G3, H2, I3: stale state that every reader ignores, or a cancellation that\n  is a no-op on every reached history.\n- D1, D3: the recompute delete filter's inner branch ran 0 times in 7,871\n  tests and in targeted histories. Recompute keeps optimistic layers for keys\n  with pending sync operations, so no such delete forms.\n\n## Limits\n\n- H3 depends on a browser idle scheduler. The suite's Node polyfill always\n  reports a timed-out deadline.\n- Source deletes run only after a batch's rows. A delete before an insert of\n  the same key in one batch is outside the grammar.\n- The driver drops a source delete for a key the source lacks, so the grammar\n  never sends one. On a plain Collection, such a delete is a silent no-op. Its\n  effect on an optimistic layer for the same key is unverified. The\n  optimistic-history oracle owns that open cell; it needs the contract for the\n  absent-key delete and a witness with an active and an accepted request on\n  the key.\n- The idle-cleanup test needs per-file module isolation, the Vitest default.\n  Without it, the binding check fails with an explicit error.\n- The fallback that derives previous `$synced`/`$origin` from completed\n  request keys still has a survivor (see the\n  [absent-key insert review](2026-10-02-insert-for-absent-key.md)).\n\n## Verification\n\n`packages/db` Vitest, typecheck off: 201 files, 7,862 tests. `tsc --noEmit`\nreports only the `tests/conformance` errors that need a built `dist`.\n"}
